  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88f6fa2b89436164b8e97b17d82dc9a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 18 - Loop
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_loop
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Loop
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: "A loop is used to repeat a group of instructions multiple times.
    Loops are useful when the same task must be performed repeatedly without rewriting
    the same code again and again. Like other code blocks, loops also require proper
    indentation. All instructions inside the loop must use the same indentation level.\n\nPrograms
    execute the instructions inside the loop from top to bottom during each repetition.
    Each repetition of a loop is called an <color=yellow>iteration</color>.\n\nExample:\n<indent=1em><font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\">LOOP_STATEMENT: <color=#6A9955># Will be explained later</color></font>\n<indent=3em><font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#33CC66>scan</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font>\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#33CC66>move</color>(<color=#CE9178>\"forward\"</color>, <color=#B5CEA8>2</color>)</font></indent></indent>\nDuring
    an iteration, the program may also control the loop using special statements:\n<indent=2em>-
    <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#D96DD3>continue</color></font> \u2192 Skip
    the remaining instructions in the current iteration and move to the next iteration</indent>\n<indent=2em>-
    <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#D96DD3>break</color></font> \u2192 Stop the
    loop completely</indent>"
  isImageBig: 0
